  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in miles per hour, we divide the number of miles, which is $3\\,450,$ by the number of hours, $6.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\,450}{6} & =3\\,450\u00f76 \\\\  & =575.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the plane is $575$ miles per hour. \n\nTo find the time it takes the plane to cover $115$ miles, we divide the distance by $575.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{115}{575} \\\\  & =\\frac{115\u00f75}{575\u00f75} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{115} \\\\  & =\\frac{23\u00f723}{115\u00f723} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the plane $0.2$ hours to travel $115$ miles.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
